First Author: Ozcan
Title: Artificial intelligence–derived cardiac ageing is associated with cardiac events post-heart transplantation
Source number: 39  ￼

Very short summary: This single-center retrospective cohort study evaluated an AI-ECG age algorithm in heart transplant recipients to determine whether post-transplant “physiological ageing” predicts adverse events. Five key findings were: (1) 540 heart transplant recipients with available pre- and post-transplant ECG data were analyzed; (2) pre-transplant ECG age averaged 63 ± 11 years and post-transplant ECG age 54 ± 10 years; (3) post-transplant ECG age correlated with both donor age and recipient age; (4) during median follow-up of 8.8 years, 307 patients experienced major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE); and (5) an increase in ECG age after transplant was independently associated with higher MACE risk, with multivariable HR 1.58 (95% CI 1.18–2.10, P = 0.002). Figure 1, Table 1, and Table 2 were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

