	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The analysis included only patients “with available pre- and post-transplantation ECG data,” which is most consistent with complete-case inclusion. The ECG-age algorithm had been previously trained on 774,783 subjects outside this study, but this paper did not retrain or provide study-specific train/test counts for the transplant cohort. Data handling was described, including averaging ECG ages from ECGs obtained within 1 year before and after HTx and excluding ECGs used in the original training/validation sets. Class imbalance is not applicable to this prognostic exposure analysis. The network architecture was “available on request,” so code availability is best classified as Other rather than Yes.  ￼

